// Test: bugfixes/list_namespace_has_only_spec_functions
// Grammar: namespace_function_call
// Semantic: FUNC001 — the `list.` namespace has only `list.concat`,
//   `list.range`, `list.fill` and `list.join` (stdlib-reference.md §5);
//   every other list operation is a method, and the error names it
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   FUNC001
//   Function 'list.add' not found
//   Call it as a method on the list: `items.add(...)` instead of `list.add(items, ...)`
//
// Regression: `list.add(l, x)`, `list.size(l)`, `list.get(l, i)` and the
// other method names compiled as namespace functions that the spec does
// not define (developer decision 0.33.184).

start:
	list<integer> numbers = [1, 2]
	list.add(numbers, 3)
	print(numbers.length())
